  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Maternal Health Equity and Accountability in Tanzania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Moving from being a child to a woman can be a difficult transition, and even more so if married at thirteen or fourteen.  When childbirth rapidly follows the risk of complications are great &#x2013; thousands of young women are physically and irreparably damaged.  In pain, incontinent and cast out by society, young girls quickly become single mothers with nowhere to turn.  This project works to raise awareness about this problem faced by thousands of young girls and tackle the reasons why this happens.  Groups of women will come together, including those already affected by this ailment and those at risk, building their skills, understanding and confidence.  Village nurses will be trained to provide support through surgery and care. The project will also works with the whole village, opening discussion and debate on child marriage.  At the same time the health officials at local and national level will be engaged, raising awareness and ensuring time and money is allocated for care. Finally, the project works at national and international level, to ensure that laws are passed to protect young women.</narrative>
  </description>
